id-to-Safe R point to a comfortable Republican margin, and prediction markets agree at roughly 12% for Democrats. The Democratic challenger's fundraising deficit and lack of polling support leave no evidence to move materially off that picture.", "watch": "Any surge in outside spending or polling showing Greene-Placentia's story shifting the race's tone could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Abraham Hamadeh (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Abraham Hamadeh seeks a full term in this R+8 Phoenix-area district, where the fundamentals strongly favor his party. Bernadette Greene-Placentia, the Democratic nominee, has raised only about $209,000 against his $1.2 million and has no polling support on record. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race Solid or Safe Republican, with a few Likely R ratings, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a 12% chance.\n\nGreene-Placentia has drawn extensive national media attention after reporting a sexual assault while repairing campaign signs, which has raised her profile. Still, with no public polls, a large money gap, and the district's partisan lean, the race remains firmly in Republican hands on paper, with the main question being the size of Hamadeh's winning margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -8.56}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0923, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0824, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1327, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0645, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0823, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0978, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0775, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1109, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0711, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0764,